Z||000000||theogre||04-20-99||10:43 PM||||This thread is for sources of clutch parts for stock, and engine upgraded, Fieros with manual tranys. While most transmissions can take a heck of alot of torque/hp most stock clutch packs can't. This means you eat alot of clutch disks, and cook off a few fly wheels real quick. (Always rememeber to replace the tranny gear oil when doing a clutch job!)<p>For a start Centerforce  <A HREF="http://www.centerforce.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.centerforce.com/</A>  stocks after market counter weighted presure plates, and dual media clutch disks, for all stock Fiero, and nearly any engine you can shoe horn into it. While the prices are signifigantly more than stock parts, you won't be replacing them any time soon.
